invariant: INV-16
file: src/p256_wide_point.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: the Jacobian doubling adds m to itself where it adds m's half, so
  m is twice (X1 - zz) (X1 + zz) where it is three halves of it, and X3
  and Y3 come out for another point. No fault follows: every coordinate
  is still a field element. bin/p256_equiv_test holds the doubling to the
  complete addition of a point with itself on multiples of G, and every
  key exchange doubles 253 times.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_half(&half, &m);
    p256_wide_fe_add(&m, &m, &half);
--- new
    p256_wide_fe_half(&half, &m);
    p256_wide_fe_add(&m, &m, &m);
